-- and an automorphism of the product composed after it: map, then relabel the product. With the
-- previous, the atom maps of a reaction carry an action of both automorphism groups, so what a
-- reaction record stores when it stores one atom map is a representative of an orbit, with the orbit
-- discarded. This is reaction degeneracy, and it is why a mechanism's rate and a map's uniqueness
-- cannot be read off the record.
am-before-auto : (L : Mol) → (R : Mol) → AtomMap L R → Auto R → AtomMap L R
am-before-auto L R m b =
  ( (λ x → auto-fun R b (am-fun L R m x))
  , (λ y → am-inv-fun L R m (auto-inv-fun R b y))
  , (λ x → concat (cong (am-inv-fun L R m) (auto-gf R b (am-fun L R m x))) (am-gf L R m x))
  , (λ y → concat (cong (auto-fun R b) (am-fg L R m (auto-inv-fun R b y))) (auto-fg R b y))
  , (λ x → concat (auto-el R b (am-fun L R m x)) (am-el L R m x)) )
